# Option byte reference used by the updater.
#   rw - compared, and patched if it differs
#   r  - compared only; a mismatch aborts the update
#   i  - ignored entirely
#
# The flash/SRAM boundaries below (SFSA, SBRV, SBRSA, SNBRSA, BRSD, NBRSD) are
# owned by FUS: it rewrites them from the wireless stack image whenever a stack
# is installed, so their values follow COPRO_STACK_BIN rather than anything we
# choose. Pinning them here only creates a failure mode - an update that swaps
# the radio stack would flash the stack, then abort on its own new option bytes.
# The radio install step already proves they are right, so they are ignored.
RDP:0xAA:r
BOR_LEV:0x4:rw
nBOOT0:0x1:rw
nBOOT1:0x1:rw
nSWBOOT0:0x1:rw
SRAM2RST:0x0:rw
SRAM2PE:0x1:rw
nRST_STOP:0x1:rw
nRST_STDBY:0x1:rw
nRSTSHDW:0x1:rw
WWDGSW:0x1:rw
IWGDSTDBY:0x1:rw
IWDGSTOP:0x1:rw
IWDGSW:0x1:rw
IPCCDBA:0x0:rw
ESE:0x1:r
SFSA:0xCE:i
FSD:0x0:r
DDS:0x1:r
C2OPT:0x1:r
NBRSD:0x0:i
SNBRSA:0xB:i
BRSD:0x0:i
SBRSA:0x12:i
SBRV:0x33800:i
PCROP1A_STRT:0x1FF:r
PCROP1A_END:0x0:r
PCROP_RDP:0x1:rw
PCROP1B_STRT:0x1FF:r
PCROP1B_END:0x0:r
WRP1A_STRT:0xFF:r
WRP1A_END:0x0:r
WRP1B_STRT:0xFF:r
WRP1B_END:0x0:r
